From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: aoss: add a free-form debugfs message entry

The AOP accepts more than the four fixed messages the qcom_aoss debugfs
exposes. In particular "{class: lpm_mon, type: cxpc, dur: 1000, flush: 5,
ts_adj: 1}" turns on the AOP's low-power-mode monitor, which logs to
message RAM which DRV (APPS, AUDIO, GPU, DISPLAY, PCIe CESTA, TZ, HYP,
L3, ...) was still voting each time CX power collapse was attempted.
The vendor kernel reads that log through its sys_pm_vx driver; this
adds only the sending half, /sys/kernel/debug/qcom_aoss/send_message,
so the log can be enabled from userspace and read back over /dev/mem.

Developer aid for the Odin 3 sleep investigation; not for upstream.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
@@ -555,7 +555,37 @@
 	.open = simple_open,
 	.write = qmp_debugfs_write,
 };
+
+/*
+ * Free-form message entry for developers: the written text is sent to the
+ * AOP verbatim, e.g. "{class: lpm_mon, type: cxpc, dur: 1000, flush: 5}".
+ */
+static ssize_t qmp_debugfs_raw_write(struct file *file, const char __user *user_buf,
+				     size_t count, loff_t *pos)
+{
+	struct qmp *qmp = file->private_data;
+	char buf[QMP_MSG_LEN];
+	ssize_t len;
+	int ret;
 
+	len = simple_write_to_buffer(buf, sizeof(buf) - 1, pos, user_buf, count);
+	if (len < 0)
+		return len;
+	buf[len] = '\0';
+	strim(buf);
+
+	ret = qmp_send(qmp, "%s", buf);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	return count;
+}
+
+static const struct file_operations qmp_debugfs_raw_fops = {
+	.open = simple_open,
+	.write = qmp_debugfs_raw_write,
+};
+
 static void qmp_debugfs_create(struct qmp *qmp)
 {
 	const struct qmp_debugfs_entry *entry;
@@ -563,6 +593,9 @@
 
 	qmp->debugfs_root = debugfs_create_dir("qcom_aoss", NULL);
 
+	debugfs_create_file("send_message", 0200, qmp->debugfs_root, qmp,
+			    &qmp_debugfs_raw_fops);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(qmp->debugfs_files); i++) {
 		entry = &qmp_debugfs_entries[i];
 
